  "step_3": "The decision reason is based on skewness — specifically, preferring a more left-skewed lottery (where favorable outcomes have higher probability). However, both lotteries are right-skewed (more probability on the zero outcome), so neither is left-skewed. Therefore, the condition for applying the reason is not met. The individual’s justification is based on the size of the gain (1000€) and the trade-off in probability, not on the skewness of the distributions. There is no mention of skewness or distribution shape in the verbal report. Thus, the individual did not use the skewness-based decision reason. Even though the reason might be relevant in a different context, it is not present in the reported reasoning. Therefore, the decision reason was not used by the individual.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
